# fixedbugs, defect 2468, lane b31-ffi, 2026-11-11: `own.h` asks
# `__has_include("cfg.h")` of the program's own `cfg.h` beside it, a name no
# platform folder holds. A file a header only asks after is judged by the
# question that finds it as an include of it is (design.md §4.19): a quoted
# spelling read from the asker's own folder, of a name the platform does not
# hold, is the program's own. Until this defect every such file was refused
# `shadowed_header` as standing in for the system's `<cfg.h>`.
#
# Corrected 2026-11-11, defect 2482: the file is `cfg2482.h`. A folder of the
# CI's Windows leg holds a `cfg.h`, so the name this case says no platform
# holds was held there, and the case refused as the system's; a name with
# that defect's number is held by no folder of this Mac's search or the
# Linux image's, and the Windows runner's is read by the CI after the push.
extern "own.h"
    constant OWN_CFG: i64

function main()
    print(OWN_CFG)
